{#
RQ3 round-one independent categorization.
Render with Jinja2 StrictUndefined. This file performs no storage or inference.

Required payload, using JSON-compatible projections:

  task_input:
    instance_id, case_id, task_name, stage, snapshot_date, task_guidance,
    source_documents, structured_feeds, candidates, environment, output_profile
    Optional: horizon_days

  evaluated_response:
    response_id, status, raw_text, parsed_answer, schema_errors

  reference_material:
    version, answer, evidence_records, applicability
    Reference evidence projections require evidence_id, role, and snippet.
    applicability contains task-specific temporal/environmental interpretation,
    not a target subtype assignment.

  frozen_taxonomy:
    taxonomy_id, iteration, guideline_hash, frozen, subtype_definitions,
    inclusion_exclusion_rules
    Definitions and rules are projected from the supplied TaxonomyVersion.
    Do not substitute config.taxonomy.published_reference.

  categorization_settings:
    rounds, first_round_independent, human_review
    Project these fields from config.categorization.
    human_review requires introduce_new_categories.
    Round-two peer_payload_policy is deliberately not required here.

  taxonomy_settings:
    multiple_labels_allowed, require_evidence_for_each_label
    Project from config.taxonomy.

  output_policy:
    allow_empty_labels_when_uncertain: explicitly resolved boolean

The output_policy is a rendering-protocol declaration, not an existing
config.yaml key. Its provenance must be recorded
through the existing configuration mechanism before formal execution.
This template supports empty uncertain assignments. A protocol forbidding them
is incompatible with its no-forced-label safeguard and blocks rendering.

All agents receive the same content packet. Agent/model identity is deliberately
absent. Assignment identifiers, actor, round, origin, and supersession are added
by orchestration, never generated by the model.

The caller must establish completed failure identification, frozen guideline
availability, reference applicability, context-budget readiness, and evidence
integrity before rendering. Templates cannot verify these storage-level facts.

Do not supply complete TaskInstance, ExperimentConfig, annotation records, peer
outputs, audit membership, target labels, or complete transformation logs.
Only the explicit projections below are rendered. Nested feeds, candidate
values, output profiles, rules, and applicability prose must be checked upstream
for accidental annotation or peer-result leakage.

Optional descriptive evidence metadata defaults to omission. Required scientific
settings have no defaults: null/missing values must fail before inference.

The reserved __rq3_round_one_invalid_payload__ symbol must never be supplied.
#}

